{"title":"Arbitrarily close","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Informally, a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> contains points <b>arbitrarily close</b> to some point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> if, for any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a63918a6fa75b62ad87ad17aaf65f782d71546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varepsilon$\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" />, there are members of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> which are less than a distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a63918a6fa75b62ad87ad17aaf65f782d71546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varepsilon$\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.  \n</p><p>More formally, in a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Metric_space\" title=\"Metric space\">metric space</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> (such as the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclidean_space\" title=\"Euclidean space\">Euclidean space</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/9/359c93f77ee9ad4fdfaae8b7c46a2d7ed91a3b29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}^n$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> or just the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a>) with distance function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Set\" title=\"Set\">set</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01cc723e511a6b312ee22de178804aa35ce512a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\subset M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> is said to contain members <b>arbitrarily close</b> to some point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dcc4457fbe6c57c7945ae191fde7c63530d291f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\in M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"16\" /> if for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/2/a42ffbf9adbf3b07afb6a1fc58005a37e9c445b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varepsilon &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> there exists some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/4045d6bc2de65aea75286ad613b46fa5a699559d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee72a7075c118891dc2db217fda5bd13f7509b22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; d(x, p) &lt; \\varepsilon$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Examples\">Examples</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arbitrarily_close&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Examples\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>In the particular case of the real numbers with the usual distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/6/1b6f04104ab0528dc99bd7d40ba58166e6d37272.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d(x, y) = |x - y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />, the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ec07b4ed63f26b23674857ca227c808024bf030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\left\\{\\frac{1}{n} \\mid n \\in \\mathbb{Z}_{&gt; 0}\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"153\" height=\"43\" /> contains points arbitrarily close to 0.</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The set of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a> contains points arbitarily close to any given real number.  This is also true of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rational_number\" title=\"Rational number\">rational numbers</a>, but it is not true of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a>.  We can see this last fact is true because (for example) there is no integer at distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8e15844d523efe58af54649ee285b2c23a96b20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" /> or less from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />.  (A set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> which contains points arbitrarily close to every point is said to be <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dense\" title=\"Dense\">dense</a>.)</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arbitrarily_close&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Arbitrarily_close&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017092001\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 116/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 292/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3315/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.650      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.650      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5212:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017092001 and revision id 31012. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}